<div><strong><em>Copula</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Something is something else</div>
    <div>noun <strong>wa</strong> noun <strong>desu</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">私<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">は</span>社長<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">です</span></div>
    <div>watashi wa shachō desu</div>
    <div>I company director am</div>
    <div>I am a company director</div>
    <div>noun <strong>wa</strong> noun <strong>de wa arimasen</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">私<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">は</span>社長<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">ではありません</span></div>
    <div>watashi wa shachō de-wa arimasen</div>
    <div>I company director am not</div>
    <div>I am not a company director</div>
</div>
<div><strong><em>Relative</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Subordinate clause that modifies a noun phrase</div>
    <div>object<em>(referent)</em> verb-<strong>ta/da</strong>(completed plain verb)<em>(relative pronoun)</em> + subject<em>(antecedent)</em></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">牛乳を<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">飲んだ</span>猫</div>
    <div>gyūnyū o nonda neko</div>
    <div>The cat that/who drank the milk</div>
</div>
<div><strong><em>Conditional</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Subordinate clause that expresses a requirement</div>
    <div>verb-<strong>nagara</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">水を飲み<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">ながら</span>新聞を読みます</div>
    <div>mizu o nominagara shinbun o yomimasu</div>
    <div>water [object] drink-while newspaper [object] read</div>
    <div>I read the newspaper while drinking water</div>
    <div>verb-<strong>aida (ni)</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">Aが水を飲んでいる<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">間に</span>Bは新聞を読んでいます</div>
    <div>A ga mizu o nondeiru aida ni B wa shinbun o yondeimasu</div>
    <div>A [subject] water [object] drinking while B [subject] newspaper [object] reading</div>
    <div>B is reading the newspaper while A is drinking the water</div>
    <div>verb-<strong>nai uchi ni</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">水を飲み<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">ない内に</span>新聞を読みます</div>
    <div>mizu o nominai uchi ni shinbun o yomimasu</div>
    <div>water [object] drink-not while newspaper [object] read</div>
    <div>I read the newspaper while not drinking water</div>
    <div>past plain verb-<strong>tara</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">(若し)水を飲ん<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">だら</span>新聞を読みます</div>
    <div>(moshi) mizu o nondara shinbun o yomimasu</div>
    <div>if water [object] drank-if newspaper [object] read</div>
    <div>If I drink the water I will read the newspaper</div>
    <div>plain verb-<strong>nakattara</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms">水を飲ま<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">なかったら</span>新聞を読みます</div>
    <div>mizu o nomanakattara shinbun o yomimasu</div>
    <div>water [object] drank-not-if newspaper [object] read</div>
    <div>If I don't drink the water I will read the newspaper</div>
</div>
